{
  "package": "io/fs",
  "notes": "Interfaces are traits (rust_stdlib::io::fs); File extends std::io::Read. Go finds optional interfaces with type assertions, which Rust trait objects cannot do, so FS has as_glob_fs/as_read_dir_fs/as_read_file_fs/as_stat_fs/as_sub_fs/as_read_link_fs hooks that an implementation overrides; Glob, ReadDir, ReadFile, Stat, Sub, Lstat and ReadLink consult them exactly where Go asserts. Errors are io::Error: a PathError is the payload (fs::path_error recovers it, its kind is the inner error's) and the sentinel variables are variants of fs::Error (Error::is is errors.Is; ERR_NOT_EXIST etc. also match by io::ErrorKind so std::fs errors qualify). Names are &str, so ValidPath's UTF-8 check is implied; WalkDirFunc is a closure trait over (path, Option<&dyn DirEntry>, Option<io::Error>) -> io::Result<()>; ReadDir returns ReadDirError, which carries the entries read before a failure (Go returns both). First-party implementations: DirFS (os.DirFS over std::fs, with ReadLinkFS), MapFS (testing/fstest.MapFS, resolving symlinks in Open, Lstat and ReadLink) and embed::FS. Tested against Go with fstest.MapFS by tools/io_check.py.",
